16
00:09:27.000 --> 00:10:21.000
to succeed in their own path. They're balancing and trading off against each other, two important and valuable dimensions of what a good and flourishing life would entail. And I think what's particularly sad about these cases is that strivers will often internalize some of the decisions they make and think of themselves as, I was a bad son or a bad sister or a bad brother or a bad friend because I ended up going to class or studying for my exam, instead of being there for this person that I love. And that's, I think, the really kind of poignant and difficult ethical position that strivers are in.

