don't fit this economic model of trade-offs is because when we love somebody, we love that particular person. You know, I have a charming three-year-old daughter who's very funny and a little loony is three-year-old to are and imagine that in the, you know, one morning I wake up and go into her room and it's not her, but it's another three-year-old who is equally funny and equally loony. And you might say, well, you lost your daughter, but there's this other equally funny, equally loony three-year-old you now get to take care of.

